  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 104.48 Source reduction",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 104.48 “Source reduction” means “source reduction” as defined in RSA 149-M:4, XXIV, namely “the practice of reducing the quantity or toxicity of waste generated at the source, before recycling, processing, disposal or treatment, by changing the processes that first generated the waste. Source reduction includes waste reduction.”\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100) #8460-B, eff 10-28-05; ss by #14103, effective 10-23-24 (formerly Env-Sw 104.41) (see Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Sw 100)",
